---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro'
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="Elixir Community privacy information.">
  <div class="container-page">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy" />
    <article class="typography mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-(--ec-muted)">Updated 7 October 2026</p>
<p>Elixir Community is run by Tomasz Tomczyk, the controller of newsletter personal data. We use your email address to send its newsletter. Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@elixir.community">hello@elixir.community</a> about your data.</p>
<h2>Signing up</h2>
<p>We ask for your email address and send a confirmation email. You must confirm before receiving the newsletter (double opt-in). We use your consent as the UK GDPR basis for newsletter emails. You can withdraw it at any time through the unsubscribe link in an email.</p>
<h2>Where your data is held</h2>
<p>Plunk holds your email address, newsletter contact record and consent status and sends our emails. Cloudflare D1 also holds your email address, confirmation nonce and status, and request timestamp. This helps prevent repeated signup requests and reuse of confirmation links.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep newsletter contact data while you are subscribed and as needed to respect an unsubscribe request. Pending, unconfirmed contacts in Plunk may remain until we delete them manually. You can ask us to delete your data.</p>
<p>Stale signup records in Cloudflare D1 are removed after 30 days when the next signup is processed. This is not a scheduled deletion exactly 30 days after a request.</p>
<h2>Email tracking</h2>
<p>Our newsletter emails do not use open or click tracking.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, restrict how it is used, or receive it in a portable format, where those rights apply. You can withdraw your newsletter consent at any time. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@elixir.community">hello@elixir.community</a>. You can also complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>
<h2>Website analytics and security</h2>
<p>Cloudflare hosts this website. We use Cloudflare Web Analytics for aggregate visits, page views and performance information, without analytics cookies. Cloudflare Turnstile checks newsletter signup requests for bots and abuse; its security checks process technical browser and network information. We use these services to understand and protect the site.</p>
<h2>Other websites</h2>
<p>Resource links take you to other websites. Their privacy policies apply there. This page describes the newsletter signup; we will update it if that process changes.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
